From: Laszlo Agocs <laszlo.agocs@qt.io>
Date: Mon, 4 Mar 2024 17:53:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] eglfs/kms: Fix having more than one window over the screen's
 lifetime

Backport of two Qt 6 commits for QTBUG-122663, squashed and adapted to
5.15 (where resetSurface() only cleared m_gbm_surface):

  818f8de64a2b "drm: Fix having more than window over the screen's lifetime"
  0a3b5042a566 "drm: atomic: Avoid device busy when flipping after creating
                a new window"

On the non-atomic path the framebuffer is bound to the CRTC once, by the
drmModeSetCrtc in ensureModeSet(), and never again. When the window that
owns the screen's gbm_surface is destroyed, the surface's buffer objects
go with it and their DRM framebuffers are removed; the kernel then
unbinds the primary plane (plane fb=0, CRTC still active). The next
QWindow's first frame goes through drmModePageFlip against an unbound
plane and gets -EBUSY, as does every frame after it: the panel stays
black while the app keeps running. Seen on vt-sbc-am62l with the
SignaSteam first-boot flow (setup wizard window, then MainWindow): the
journal fills with "Could not queue DRM page flip on screen DSI1 (Device
or resource busy)" from the moment MainWindow is shown.

With this change resetSurface() asks for a fresh drmModeSetCrtc the next
time a frame is flipped, which rebinds the plane to the new window's
framebuffer. The m_flipPending/m_gbm_bo_current reset is the 5.15
equivalent of the second commit's cleanup.

Upstream-Status: Backport [Qt 6.5, 818f8de64a2b1a7371ecb4bdd527b05343190582 + 0a3b5042a566afa4dc5162f469eb0d8be3120933]
Signed-off-by: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>
---
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/eglfs/deviceintegration/eglfs_kms/qeglfskmsgbmscreen.cpp	2026-10-23 10:36:59.905098252 -0500
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/eglfs/deviceintegration/eglfs_kms/qeglfskmsgbmscreen.cpp	2026-10-23 10:36:59.931616783 -0500
@@ -196,7 +196,19 @@
 
 void QEglFSKmsGbmScreen::resetSurface()
 {
+    m_flipPending = false; // not necessarily true but enough to keep bo_next
+    m_gbm_bo_current = nullptr;
     m_gbm_surface = nullptr;
+
+    // Leave m_gbm_bo_next untouched. waitForFlip() should
+    // still do its work, when called. Otherwise we end up
+    // in device-is-busy errors if there is a new QWindow
+    // created afterwards. (QTBUG-122663)
+
+    // If not using atomic, will need a new drmModeSetCrtc if a new window
+    // gets created later on (and so there's a new fb).
+    if (!device()->hasAtomicSupport())
+        needsNewModeSetForNextFb = true;
 }
 
 void QEglFSKmsGbmScreen::initCloning(QPlatformScreen *screenThisScreenClones,
@@ -224,8 +236,9 @@
     QKmsOutput &op(output());
     const int fd = device()->fd();
 
-    if (!op.mode_set) {
+    if (!op.mode_set || needsNewModeSetForNextFb) {
         op.mode_set = true;
+        needsNewModeSetForNextFb = false;
 
         bool doModeSet = true;
         drmModeCrtcPtr currentMode = drmModeGetCrtc(fd, op.crtc_id);
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/eglfs/deviceintegration/eglfs_kms/qeglfskmsgbmscreen.h	2026-10-23 10:36:59.913085804 -0500
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/eglfs/deviceintegration/eglfs_kms/qeglfskmsgbmscreen.h	2026-10-23 10:36:59.932214145 -0500
@@ -105,6 +105,8 @@
         bool cloneFlipPending = false;
     };
     QVector<CloneDestination> m_cloneDests;
+
+    bool needsNewModeSetForNextFb = false;
 };
 
 QT_END_NAMESPACE
